      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Alert on weather risk for upcoming outdoor bookings\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs a daily check for upcoming outdoor bookings, filters bookings into a lookahead window, and retrieves location-specific weather forecasts. It computes a weather risk level, then branches into moderate-risk owner notifications or severe-risk customer and owner notifications. For severe risks, it avoids re-notifying customers who were already alerted while still updating the owner and Airtable status.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the schedule trigger frequency and timezone for the daily weather check.\n- Set the Airtable base ID, bookings table name, WhatsApp phone number ID, and owner Slack channel ID in the Set Configuration node.\n- Connect Airtable credentials with read/write access to the bookings table.\n- Connect Slack credentials and confirm the owner alert channel is valid.\n- Connect WhatsApp/Meta credentials and ensure approved message templates or outbound messaging permissions are available.\n- Verify the booking table contains the fields expected by the filter, risk computation, notification, and Airtable update nodes, such as booking date/time, location, customer phone, risk status, and customer-notified flag.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the lookahead window, weather risk thresholds, notification wording, and Airtable status fields to match the business rules for different outdoor activities or regions."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
